---
/* The Tree Canvas on its own: recordatlas.org/tree-canvas/. The same canvas that is the first tab of Roots & Routes, with "brought to you by Record
   Atlas" in its title and an "Open GEDCOM" button on the right. It is not the Base layout (which carries a counter, an ad slot and Google Fonts) for
   the same reason /roots/ is not: the file never leaves the device, and the meta CSP below is the browser enforcing that. The page around the
   canvas (public/tree-canvas/app.js) reads the file with the roots page's own reader (public/roots/js/worker.js) and hands the tree to the canvas
   in memory, as /roots/ does; nothing is stored. */
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; frame-src 'self'; form-action 'none'; base-uri 'none'">
<meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<title>Tree Canvas · Record Atlas</title>
<meta name="description" content="Draw your family tree from a GEDCOM file on one canvas, with the Record Atlas's places, rulers and record collections for each person. Read in your browser, never uploaded.">
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/tree-canvas/page.css">
</head>
<body>
<main id="start" aria-labelledby="stTitle">
  <h1 id="stTitle">Tree Canvas</h1>
  <p class="stlead">Draw your family tree on one canvas, with the Atlas's places, rulers and record collections for each person. Your file is read in this browser and never uploaded.</p>
  <div class="stbtns">
    <button type="button" class="stbtn primary" id="stOpen">Open your GEDCOM</button>
    <button type="button" class="stbtn" id="stDemo">Open an invented family example</button>
  </div>
  <input type="file" id="stFile" accept=".ged,.gedcom,.txt,text/plain" hidden>
  <section id="stRecent" class="strec" hidden aria-labelledby="stRecTitle">
    <h2 id="stRecTitle">Last used</h2>
    <ul id="stList"></ul>
    <p class="stnote">Kept in this browser only, so you can open them again in one click. <button type="button" class="stlink" id="stForget">Forget them all</button></p>
  </section>
</main>
<iframe id="cv" title="Tree Canvas, drawn from your GEDCOM" hidden></iframe>
<p id="msg" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
<noscript><p class="nojs">The Tree Canvas needs JavaScript to read your file in this browser. Nothing is uploaded. <a href="/">Back to Record Atlas</a></p></noscript>
<script is:inline src="/tree-canvas/app.js" type="module"></script>
</body>
</html>
